// "e3john": "john3", "jude": "jude"

const SCRIPTURE_B13 = [
{
id: "corinthians2-4", name: "2 Corinthians 4 \u2014 The Inward Man", testament: "NT", order: 139,
intro: "The outward man decays, the inward man renews \u2014 and affliction weighed against eternity.",
chapters: [
{ n: 4, verses: [
{ n: 16, t: "For which cause we faint not; but though our outward man perish, yet the inward man is renewed day by day.", note: "Your OUTWARD man \u2014 the body, the face in the mirror \u2014 is perishing. That's not tragedy, that's biology. Your INWARD man \u2014 the real you, the awareness behind the eyes \u2014 gets RENEWED daily. Translation: stop feeding the decaying one and start feeding the eternal one. What you feed is what grows." },
{ n: 17, t: "For our light affliction, which is but for a moment, worketh for us a far more exceeding and eternal weight of glory;", note: "'LIGHT affliction' \u2014 Paul calls his beatings, shipwrecks, and imprisonments LIGHT. Not because they didn't hurt, but because he weighed them against 'an eternal weight of glory' and they came up feathers. The teaching's scale: put today's trouble on one side, eternity on the other, and watch the trouble float. Perspective is the whole trick." },
{ n: 18, t: "While we look not at the things which are seen, but at the things which are not seen: for the things which are seen are temporal; but the things which are not seen are eternal.", note: "Look NOT at the seen \u2014 the bank account, the diagnosis, the circumstance \u2014 because it's TEMPORAL: it's got an expiration date. Look at the UNSEEN, because that's ETERNAL. This isn't denial; it's investment strategy. You get more of whatever you stare at, so stare at the permanent stuff." },
] },
{ n: 5, verses: [
{ n: 17, t: "Therefore if any man be in Christ, he is a new creature: old things are passed away; behold, all things are become new.", note: "'If any man be IN CHRIST, he is a NEW CREATURE.' Not a repaired creature, not an improved creature \u2014 NEW. 'Old things are PASSED AWAY.' The teaching's reading: your past is not your identity, it's your compost. The new thing doesn't grow out of the old thing's permission \u2014 it grows the moment you step into it." },
] },
],
},
{
id: "thessalonians1-4", name: "1 Thessalonians 4 \u2014 Rejoice Evermore", testament: "NT", order: 140,
intro: "Caught up to meet the Lord \u2014 and the three-command program: joy, prayer, thanks.",
chapters: [
{ n: 4, verses: [
{ n: 16, t: "For the Lord himself shall descend from heaven with a shout, with the voice of the archangel, and with the trump of God: and the dead in Christ shall rise first:", note: "'The dead in Christ shall RISE FIRST.' The teaching's inner reading: the dead parts of you \u2014 buried hopes, numb places, shelved dreams \u2014 wake up BEFORE the living parts ascend. Resurrection starts underground. Don't skip the graveyard on the way up; that's where the rising begins." },
{ n: 17, t: "Then we which are alive and remain shall be caught up together with them in the clouds, to meet the Lord in the air: and so shall we ever be with the Lord.", note: "'Caught up... to meet the Lord IN THE AIR.' The 'air' is the atmosphere of thought \u2014 the meeting happens in consciousness, not in the clouds. 'And so shall we EVER BE with the Lord' \u2014 the end of the story isn't a visit, it's a residence. The ascension isn't a trip; it's a move." },
] },
{ n: 5, verses: [
{ n: 16, t: "Rejoice evermore.", note: "Two words. 'Rejoice EVERMORE' \u2014 not when you feel like it, not when things improve: evermore. Joy as a discipline, not a mood. The teaching's defiance: the world sets your circumstances; you set your rejoicing. Evermore means evermore." },
{ n: 17, t: "Pray without ceasing.", note: "'Pray WITHOUT CEASING.' Not scheduled prayer \u2014 ceaseless prayer: the running conversation underneath the day. Brother Lawrence called it practicing the presence. The teaching's method: turn the monologue in your head into a dialogue with heaven, and never hang up." },
{ n: 18, t: "In every thing give thanks: for this is the will of God in Christ Jesus concerning you.", note: "'IN EVERY THING give thanks' \u2014 in, not for: you don't thank God FOR the disaster, you thank him IN it. 'For this is the WILL OF GOD' \u2014 you want to know God's will for your life? It's right here: joy, prayer, gratitude, on repeat. The whole program in three verses." },
] },
],
},
{
id: "thessalonians2-2", name: "2 Thessalonians 2 \u2014 Stand Fast", testament: "NT", order: 141,
intro: "Hold the teaching you were given \u2014 and the faithful Lord who steadies you.",
chapters: [
{ n: 2, verses: [
{ n: 15, t: "Therefore, brethren, stand fast, and hold the traditions which ye have been taught, whether by word, or our epistle.", note: "'STAND FAST, and HOLD the traditions.' Traditions here isn't dead religion \u2014 it's the handed-down teaching, the stuff that worked. In an age of spiritual novelty every five minutes, the command is beautifully boring: hold what you were taught. The teaching's anchor: depth beats novelty. Stand fast." },
] },
{ n: 3, verses: [
{ n: 3, t: "But the Lord is faithful, who shall stablish you, and keep you from evil.", note: "'The Lord is FAITHFUL, who shall STABLISH you.' Stablish \u2014 old word for stabilize, make steady. You don't have to hold yourself together; you're being HELD together. The keeping isn't your grip on God \u2014 it's his grip on you. Rest in the grip." },
] },
],
},
{
id: "timothy1-4", name: "1 Timothy 4 \u2014 The Example", testament: "NT", order: 142,
intro: "Too young to be written off \u2014 and the wealth formula nobody preaches.",
chapters: [
{ n: 4, verses: [
{ n: 12, t: "Let no man despise thy youth; but be thou an example of the believers, in word, in conversation, in charity, in spirit, in faith, in purity.", note: "'Let no man DESPISE THY YOUTH.' Timothy was young and people wrote him off \u2014 Paul's answer isn't 'wait your turn,' it's 'be undeniable.' 'Be thou an EXAMPLE... in word, in conversation [conduct], in charity, in spirit, in faith, in purity.' Six arenas. You don't argue your way into respect; you live your way into it. Example beats explanation." },
] },
{ n: 6, verses: [
{ n: 6, t: "But godliness with contentment is great gain.", note: "'Godliness WITH CONTENTMENT is great gain.' The whole prosperity gospel in reverse: gain isn't godliness plus STUFF, it's godliness plus ENOUGH. Contentment is the multiplier \u2014 without it, no amount is gain; with it, a little is a fortune. The teaching's wealth formula: want what you have, and you're rich." },
] },
],
},
{
id: "timothy2-1", name: "2 Timothy 1 \u2014 No Spirit of Fear", testament: "NT", order: 143,
intro: "Fear is an intruder, not an inheritance \u2014 and Paul's last words from death row.",
chapters: [
{ n: 1, verses: [
{ n: 7, t: "For God hath not given us the spirit of fear; but of power, and of love, and of a sound mind.", note: "'God hath NOT given us the SPIRIT OF FEAR.' Read that again: fear is not from God. If it's not from God, it's an intruder \u2014 treat it like one. What you DID get: 'POWER, and LOVE, and a SOUND MIND.' Power for the fight, love for the people, a sound mind for the decisions. Fear is the counterfeit; this is the currency." },
] },
{ n: 4, verses: [
{ n: 7, t: "I have fought a good fight, I have finished my course, I have kept the faith:", note: "Paul's last words, from a death cell: 'I have FOUGHT a good fight, I have FINISHED my course, I have KEPT the faith.' Three past tenses \u2014 fought, finished, kept. No regrets about the outcome, only the faithfulness. The teaching's finish line: you don't have to win every round. Fight the good one, finish YOUR course, keep the faith. That's the whole r\u00e9sum\u00e9." },
] },
],
},
{
id: "titus2", name: "Titus 2 \u2014 Grace Teaching", testament: "NT", order: 144,
intro: "Grace appeared to all \u2014 and it teaches you to say no. Plus the washing of regeneration.",
chapters: [
{ n: 2, verses: [
{ n: 11, t: "For the grace of God that bringeth salvation hath appeared to all men,", note: "'The GRACE of God... hath appeared to ALL MEN' \u2014 grace isn't a members-only deal, it's appeared to all. Not earned, not exclusive, not gated. If grace appeared to all men, then no one you meet is outside its reach \u2014 including you, on your worst day." },
{ n: 12, t: "Teaching us that, denying ungodliness and worldly lusts, we should live soberly, righteously, and godly, in this present world;", note: "Grace TEACHES: 'denying ungodliness and worldly lusts, we should live soberly, righteously, and godly.' Grace isn't permission to coast \u2014 it's the teacher that trains you to say no. Real grace makes you stricter with yourself, not looser. If your 'grace' never says no to anything, it isn't grace \u2014 it's an excuse with a halo." },
] },
{ n: 3, verses: [
{ n: 5, t: "Not by works of righteousness which we have done, but according to his mercy he saved us, by the washing of regeneration, and renewing of the Holy Ghost;", note: "'NOT by works of righteousness which we have done, but according to his MERCY.' Your r\u00e9sum\u00e9 didn't save you; his mercy did. 'The WASHING of REGENERATION' \u2014 re-genesis, a second beginning: you get washed and restarted. The teaching's reset button: no one is past a fresh start. No one." },
] },
],
},
{
id: "philemon", name: "Philemon \u2014 The Runaway", testament: "NT", order: 145,
intro: "The whole letter in four verses: a runaway slave sent home \u2014 as a brother.",
chapters: [
{ n: 1, verses: [
{ n: 10, t: "I beseech thee for my son Onesimus, whom I have begotten in my bonds:", note: "Onesimus was a RUNAWAY slave. Paul \u2014 himself in chains \u2014 calls him 'my SON, whom I have begotten in my BONDS.' The prisoner fathers the runaway. The teaching: your lowest place can become someone else's birthplace. Chains don't disqualify you from fathering freedom." },
{ n: 11, t: "Which in time past was to thee unprofitable, but now profitable to thee and to me:", note: "'In time past UNPROFITABLE, but NOW PROFITABLE.' The name Onesimus literally means 'profitable, useful' \u2014 the runaway finally living up to his name. Your worst chapter can become your namesake chapter. Unprofitable is a season, not a sentence." },
{ n: 15, t: "For perhaps he therefore departed for a season, that thou shouldest receive him for ever;", note: "'Perhaps he DEPARTED FOR A SEASON, that thou shouldest receive him FOR EVER.' The temporary loss, reframed as permanent gain: the running away was the setup for the coming home. The teaching's long view: some departures are just long hallways to a better reunion. 'Perhaps' \u2014 Paul leaves room for mystery, and so should you." },
{ n: 16, t: "Not now as a servant, but above a servant, a brother beloved, specially to me, but how much more unto thee, both in the flesh, and in the Lord?", note: "'Not now as a SERVANT, but above a servant, a BROTHER BELOVED.' Paul doesn't just ask Philemon to forgive the runaway \u2014 he asks him to UPGRADE him: from property to brother. The teaching's social dynamite: in Christ the hierarchy flattens. No one is beneath you; everyone's family." },
] },
],
},
{
id: "peter2-1", name: "2 Peter 1 \u2014 Partakers", testament: "NT", order: 146,
intro: "Sharers of the divine nature \u2014 and God's clock, which doesn't tick like yours.",
chapters: [
{ n: 1, verses: [
{ n: 4, t: "Whereby are given unto us exceeding great and precious promises: that by these ye might be partakers of the divine nature, having escaped the corruption that is in the world through lust.", note: "'That by these ye might be PARTAKERS OF THE DIVINE NATURE.' Read it slowly: partakers \u2014 sharers \u2014 of the DIVINE nature. Not admirers of it, not students of it \u2014 PARTAKERS. 'Having ESCAPED the corruption that is in the world through lust.' The escape hatch from corruption isn't willpower \u2014 it's participation: you get out of the mud by taking on a different nature." },
] },
{ n: 3, verses: [
{ n: 8, t: "But, beloved, be not ignorant of this one thing, that one day is with the Lord as a thousand years, and a thousand years as one day.", note: "'One day is with the Lord AS A THOUSAND YEARS, and a thousand years as one day.' God's clock doesn't tick like yours. The teaching's patience pill: what feels like divine delay is divine timelessness. He's not late \u2014 he's not ON your schedule at all. A thousand years is a day to him; your worst waiting season is his coffee break." },
] },
],
},
{
id: "e1john1", name: "1 John 1 \u2014 God Is Light", testament: "NT", order: 147,
intro: "No darkness at all \u2014 the cleansing that runs while you walk \u2014 and God is love.",
chapters: [
{ n: 1, verses: [
{ n: 5, t: "This then is the message which we have heard of him, and declare unto you, that God is light, and in him is no darkness at all.", note: "'God is LIGHT, and in him is NO DARKNESS AT ALL.' Not 'mostly light' \u2014 NO darkness at all. Zero. Which means anything dark in your life isn't from him \u2014 it's the absence of him, like cold is the absence of heat. The teaching's diagnostic: if it's dark, it's not God. Walk toward the light." },
{ n: 7, t: "But if we walk in the light, as he is in the light, we have fellowship one with another, and the blood of Jesus Christ his Son cleanseth us from all sin.", note: "'If we WALK in the light... the blood of Jesus Christ his Son CLEANSETH us from all sin.' Cleanseth \u2014 present tense, ongoing: the cleansing runs WHILE you walk, not after you arrive. You don't get clean then walk; you walk and get cleaned. And notice the fellowship comes first \u2014 the light connects you to people before it perfects you." },
{ n: 9, t: "If we confess our sins, he is faithful and just to forgive us our sins, and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness.", note: "'If we CONFESS our sins, he is FAITHFUL and JUST to forgive.' Faithful AND just \u2014 forgiving you isn't God bending the rules, it's him KEEPING them. Confession isn't groveling; it's agreeing with the truth and letting the wash run. 'Cleanse us from ALL unrighteousness' \u2014 all of it. No fine print." },
] },
{ n: 4, verses: [
{ n: 8, t: "He that loveth not knoweth not God; for God is love.", note: "'God is LOVE.' Not 'God loves' \u2014 God IS. Love isn't something he does; it's what he IS. Which makes 'he that loveth not KNOWETH NOT God' the bluntest verse in the Bible: lovelessness isn't a personality flaw, it's unfamiliarity with God. Want to know him? Practice the thing he is." },
{ n: 16, t: "And we have known and believed the love that God hath to us. God is love; and he that dwelleth in love dwelleth in God, and God in him.", note: "'He that DWELLETH in love DWELLETH in God, and God in him.' The address of God isn't a building \u2014 it's love itself. Move into love and you've moved into God; God moves into you right back. Double occupancy. The teaching's whole theology in one verse: the zip code of heaven is love." },
] },
],
},
{
id: "e2john", name: "2 John \u2014 Truth and Love", testament: "NT", order: 148,
intro: "The shortest book in the Bible \u2014 thirteen verses on walking in truth and loving one another.",
chapters: [
{ n: 1, verses: [
{ n: 4, t: "I rejoiced greatly that I found of thy children walking in truth, as we have received a commandment from the Father.", note: "'I rejoiced GREATLY that I found of thy children WALKING IN TRUTH.' John's greatest joy isn't their success, their growth, their numbers \u2014 it's that they're walking in truth. Walking \u2014 not arrived, not perfected: walking. Direction over perfection, every time." },
{ n: 5, t: "And now I beseech thee, lady, not as though I wrote a new commandment unto thee, but that which we had from the beginning, that we love one another.", note: "'Not... a NEW commandment... but that which we had FROM THE BEGINNING, that we LOVE ONE ANOTHER.' The oldest command is still the current assignment. No updates, no upgrades, no new revelation needed: love one another. The teaching's reminder: you're not behind because you haven't found the secret \u2014 you're behind because you haven't done the obvious." },
{ n: 6, t: "And this is love, that we walk after his commandments. This is the commandment, That, as ye have heard from the beginning, ye should walk in it.", note: "'THIS is love, that we WALK after his commandments.' Love isn't a feeling here \u2014 it's a direction. A walk. Truth without love is a weapon; love without truth is a fog. John holds both in one hand: walk in truth, and let the walking BE the love." },
] },
],
},
{
id: "e3john", name: "3 John \u2014 Prosper and Be in Health", testament: "NT", order: 149,
intro: "God's will for your body and your bank account \u2014 measured by your soul.",
chapters: [
{ n: 1, verses: [
{ n: 2, t: "Beloved, I wish above all things that thou mayest prosper and be in health, even as thy soul prospereth.", note: "'I wish above all things that thou mayest PROSPER and BE IN HEALTH, even as thy soul prospereth.' God's will includes your prosperity AND your health \u2014 and the measure is your SOUL's prosperity. The teaching's order: soul first, then the rest follows the soul's size. A prosperous soul in a sick body is the anomaly; health follows the inner life." },
{ n: 4, t: "I have no greater joy than to hear that my children walk in truth.", note: "'I have NO GREATER JOY than to hear that my children WALK IN TRUTH.' Same joy as 2 John \u2014 the apostle's happiness has one source: people he loves, walking straight. Not their comfort, not their applause \u2014 their truth-walk. Check what gives YOU the greatest joy; it reveals what you worship." },
{ n: 11, t: "Beloved, follow not that which is evil, but that which is good. He that doeth good is of God: but he that doeth evil hath not seen God.", note: "'Follow NOT that which is evil, but that which is GOOD. He that DOETH GOOD is of God.' Walk in truth (v.4), do good (v.11) \u2014 the whole discipleship program in a postcard. You don't need a more complicated spiritual life. You need a more obedient one. And note the test is doing, not knowing: 'he that DOETH.'" },
] },
],
},
{
id: "jude", name: "Jude \u2014 Kept From Falling", testament: "NT", order: 150,
intro: "Build yourself up, stay in the love \u2014 and the One who is able to keep you.",
chapters: [
{ n: 1, verses: [
{ n: 20, t: "But ye, beloved, building up yourselves on your most holy faith, praying in the Holy Ghost,", note: "'BUILDING UP YOURSELVES on your most holy faith, PRAYING in the Holy Ghost.' Building up \u2014 construction, daily, by you: faith is built like a house, not found like a coin. 'Praying in the Holy Ghost' \u2014 prayer from the spirit, not the script: groans, fire, honesty, not performance. Build with your hands, pray with your spirit." },
{ n: 21, t: "Keep yourselves in the love of God, looking for the mercy of our Lord Jesus Christ unto eternal life.", note: "'KEEP YOURSELVES in the love of God.' Stay inside it like a house \u2014 don't wander out into the cold of performance, shame, or striving. 'Looking for the MERCY of our Lord Jesus Christ unto eternal life' \u2014 the gaze is forward, on mercy, not backward on failure. Kept in love, looking at mercy: that's the posture." },
{ n: 24, t: "Now unto him that is able to keep you from falling, and to present you faultless before the presence of his glory with exceeding joy,", note: "'Unto him that is ABLE TO KEEP YOU FROM FALLING.' He is ABLE \u2014 the keeping is his job, not yours. 'Present you FAULTLESS before the presence of his glory' \u2014 not 'present you with a list of improvements.' Faultless. 'With EXCEEDING JOY' \u2014 his joy, at presenting you. The teaching's ending: you're kept, you'll be presented spotless, and heaven throws a party about it." },
] },
],
},
];
